# Types for the two file objects this port owns outright.

# The mini-HDMI debugfs node, labelled in genfs_contexts. debugfs_type carries
# the platform's debugfs neverallows (no executables there, and so on) while
# keeping it out of the blanket generic-debugfs ban.
type xdplus_debugfs_hdmi, fs_type, debugfs_type;

# ⚠️ /data/vkshim deliberately has NO type of its own, and cannot get one.
#
# It is a single directory that vkshim writes to from inside every app process.
# A custom type fails the build: app_neverallows.te forbids every untrusted app
# from `create`/`unlink` on any type outside the per-app sandbox set. Keeping
# system_data_file fails too, because domain.te neverallows a new domain from
# writing or unlinking that type -- so the boot-time budget prune cannot be
# granted either.
#
# Under enforcement, therefore, both halves of the shader cache stop working:
# apps cannot write their .pcache and xdplus_tweaks cannot prune the directory.
# The fix is a design change in vkshim -- put each cache inside the app's own
# sandbox, where app_data_file access already exists -- not a policy rule.
